// fixe_nm holds strings, so the sum that witnesses an lset into an int column
// has no equivalent here: counting the entries that have been given a name
// does the same work, since fix_name_at (../../name.id) ssets a name into a
// cell that already exists and leaves the column's length alone. It reports
// how many events are named, not which, and a name replaced by a different
// name would not move it. Its own two cases cannot discriminate: fix_name_at
// is the only writer that puts a real name in the column -- fix_push4 pushes
// "" -- so no setup leaves one there to read.
fixe_nm_named() {
  int n = 0;
  int i = 0;
  while(i < len((import fixe_nm))) {
    if((import fixe_nm)[i] != "") {
      n = n + 1;
    }
    i = i + 1;
  }
} return int n;
